From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: hy200-qz713df-a1: the case power button

Stock wires the case power button to PL4 as KEY_POWER and a wakeup source:
keyboard@2009800 carries power-key = <KEY_POWER> and power-gpio = PL4, and
standby_param names power_key = "PL4" with a 50 ms debounce. Our DT left
the pin unclaimed and its function disabled.

Measured on the bench board on 2026-10-07: as an input, PL4 reads high 200
of 200 samples with the internal pull off, up and down, so it is pulled up
on the board; three short presses gave three clean low pulses of 210-290 ms
with no bounce at 2 ms polling. So the key is active low, whatever stock's
flag cell says (its own keyboard driver interprets that).

Describe it with gpio-keys. The projector board is left alone until its DT
is audited against the hardware.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include "sun50i-h713.dtsi"
+#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
 
 / {
 	model = "HY200 QZ713DF_A1 (Allwinner H713)";
@@ -18,6 +19,25 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * The case power button. Stock wires it to PL4 as KEY_POWER and a
+	 * wakeup source (keyboard@2009800 power-gpio, standby_param
+	 * power_key, 50 ms debounce). On this board PL4 reads high under
+	 * every internal pull, so it is pulled up externally, and a press
+	 * drives it low (three presses, 2026-10-07).
+	 */
+	gpio-keys {
+		compatible = "gpio-keys";
+
+		key-power {
+			label = "Power";
+			gpios = <&r_pio 0 4 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PL4 */
+			linux,code = <KEY_POWER>;
+			debounce-interval = <50>;
+			wakeup-source;
+		};
+	};
+
 	h713-edid-clock-hold {
 		compatible = "h713-lab,edid-clock-hold";
 		clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_R_EDID>;
